Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:44:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 243/260] [ae-patch] Keep a Claude session's transcript on a
 cold relaunch when it already covers the server

Every cold relaunch rewrote ~/.claude/projects/<dir>/<sid>.jsonl from server items.
The rebuilt bytes differ from what Claude sent before, so the next call wrote the whole
history to the prompt cache again. The transcript on disk is now kept when it can be
resumed and every toolu_ call id and the last user text of the server items appear in
it, or copied from an old workspace dir under the same check, and rebuilt otherwise.

The forwarder cursor is read before the launch wipes it, so a kept file that is ahead of
the server is forwarded from where the cursor stopped; with no usable cursor the file
must match the server exactly. The path taken is labelled ae.claude_native.resume
(kept, copied or rebuilt) with a running ae.claude_native.resume_count.
